# Line-ending rules git enforces for every checkout, on every machine.
#
# TEACHING NOTE: Windows uses CRLF line endings, Linux uses LF. Git can
# auto-convert — which is usually helpful and occasionally catastrophic:
# a shell script checked out with CRLF endings starts with "#!/bin/sh\r",
# and Linux looks for an interpreter literally named "sh\r". Boot failure
# inside Docker, invisible in the editor. These rules pin the files where
# endings MATTER to LF everywhere, no matter who checks out where.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.mp4 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
